  "interpretation": [
    "Planar momentum and signed work ledgers remain numerically consistent; active support command fractions remain <=1 up to roundoff. These checks do not validate unrepresented vertical/limb energy or the viscous motor law.",
    "Shared native12-vs48 mean/max trajectory disagreement worsens from .02970/.06903 yd to .12935/1.32301 yd; the strongest deterioration is jam/strong and jam/heavy. These probes have no leg grasps, isolating a support correction/stance-allocation failure.",
    "Cumulative support offset reaches3.927 yd in two-second shared probes without leg holds,6.366 yd in tracking games and7.267 yd in eight-game guards. Because graspPoint uses offset as a contact endpoint, the coordinate needs support transfer/localization before it can represent a reachable foot contact.",
    "Ordinary frontal tackling is preserved; mirrored30-degree4-yd/s misses become tackles. Football missed+broken tackle rate nevertheless worsens from.25 to.28/play against the published production baseline. Isolated success is not established tackle realism.",
    "Pressure and sacks move nearer NFL references, but closer league statistics do not establish physical or population validity. Profiles and controllers are not retuned; roster and play histories diverge after physical outcomes differ.",
    "Final shared/hand experimental trajectories exactly match the earlier experiment. This is evidence for unchanged tested active branches, not proof of unmeasured full-game trajectory equivalence; the experimental4/8 measurements retain their original source pin.",
    "Elapsed time includes observational telemetry and concurrent diagnostics; it is not a controlled performance comparison."
  ],
